---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import "../styles/excel-reporting.css";
---
<Layout title="Website privacy | Trellis Works" description="How the Trellis Works Excel reporting page handles booking, email enquiries and campaign information.">
  <main id="main" class="report-container report-section" style="max-width:760px;min-height:75vh">
    <p class="report-eyebrow">Website privacy · November 19, 2026</p><h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.8rem,6vw,4rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin-bottom:32px">A simple way to start a conversation.</h1>
    <div style="display:grid;gap:26px">
      <section><h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:10px">Booking and enquiries</h2><p>The reporting page does not collect or upload spreadsheets. Booking links open Google Appointment Schedules, where you provide your details to arrange a call. Google’s privacy terms apply to that service. Email links open a draft in your email service; nothing is sent until you send it.</p></section>
      <section><h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:10px">Information you choose to share</h2><p>We use information you provide through booking or email to respond to your enquiry and discuss the proposed work. Start with a description of your workflow. We agree an appropriate sharing and handling process before receiving business files. Do not include passwords or sensitive client records in an initial enquiry.</p></section>
      <section><h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:10px">Website and campaign information</h2><p>Cloudflare hosts this website and processes standard connection information to serve and protect it. Campaign URLs may contain labels identifying an ad or campaign. On the Excel reporting page, you can allow or decline OpenAI ad measurement. Until you allow it, we do not load the OpenAI measurement pixel. If you allow it, the pixel sends page views and booking-button clicks to OpenAI to help measure our ChatGPT ads. It processes browser and connection information and uses first-party cookies, including an ad-click reference (up to 30 days) and a browser reference (up to 365 days). Browser restrictions or clearing cookies may shorten these lifetimes. The pixel may automatically hash supported contact information if present on the page; our reporting page has no contact-entry form. The website pixel does not manually send names, email addresses, report contents or appointment details. Booking clicks do not confirm that an appointment was booked. You can change your choice using “Ad measurement settings” on the reporting page; declining turns off future website-pixel measurement and instructs the pixel to remove its attribution cookies. Your choice is saved in your browser. See <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI’s privacy policy</a> for its handling of measurement data.</p></section>
      <section><h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:10px">Booking measurement</h2><p>When someone books a report-automation scoping call, we tell OpenAI that a call was booked. We also send a scrambled version of their email address, called a hash, so OpenAI can try to connect the booking to one of our ChatGPT ads. We do not send their actual email address, name, meeting notes or answers to the booking questions. A booking is counted as an ad result only if OpenAI can match it. The ad-measurement buttons on our website control the website pixel only; they do not turn this separate booking measurement on or off.</p></section>
      <section><h2 style="font-size:1.4rem;margin-bottom:10px">Questions</h2><p>For questions about information you have shared with Trellis Works, contact <a class="text-link" style="margin-top:0" href="mailto:info@trellisworks.ca">info@trellisworks.ca</a>.</p></section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <footer class="report-footer"><div class="report-container footer-row"><a href="/">Trellis Works</a><a href="/excel-reporting/">Excel reporting automation</a></div></footer>
</Layout>
